# Code owners for go-service-kit.
#
# This module is imported by every Rebuy Go service, so a change here ships to all
# of them at once. Owners are the people who actually write Go here — named
# individuals rather than a team, deliberately: the Go contributor set does not map
# onto any existing GitHub team, and pointing at `devops` would route reviews to
# people who do not work in this language.
#
# ── What this file does, and what it does not ────────────────────────────────
#
# It AUTO-REQUESTS review from the owners on every PR. It does NOT block merge:
# `main` runs the standard protection tier — 1 approval, `devops` in
# `pull_request_bypassers` — set in the github-rbac stack in shared-infrastructure.
#
# Enforcing owner review would mean `require_code_owner_reviews = true`, which in
# that module exists only on the STRICT tier. Strict also defaults to 2 approvals,
# against the standing 1-approval-max direction. Deliberately not taken.
#
# ⚠️ What makes merging work here is the guild holding `maintain`, not `push`.
# restrict_pushes is on under the standard tier with an empty allow-list, and DO-388
# established that write-role users cannot merge in that configuration — merge is a
# push to the base branch, and the floor is maintain-and-up. senator-rebuy hit
# exactly this on admin-nextjs #53, which is a standard-tier repo; the fix was
# raising his role, not changing tier.
#
# (An earlier version of this file attributed that to the strict tier. It was wrong;
# corrected 2026-08-19.)
#
# ── Owners ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The backend guild, which is chartered as "merged PHP + Go guilds — maintainers of
# shared backend libraries". This repo is one of those libraries, so the guild is the
# owner rather than a hand-listed set of individuals: a team roster is maintained in
# one place (the github-rbac stack) and survives people moving between pods, which a
# list of handles here would not.
#
# The guild holds `maintain` on this repo, which is what lets them merge — `push`
# cannot, under the standard tier (DO-388).

*       @rebuyengine/backend-guild
